IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saz-law`

-- Seat layer: a soldier serving within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
-- It asks that soldier's questions, takes plain facts as inputs, builds the law layer's record internally and calls the law layer's rules.
-- It restates no rule. Target compiler: main.
-- A field of the law layer's record that no question here reads gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment: `has a long-term working-time account` is FALSE below,
-- because none of this layer's questions asks about long-term accounts (the law layer has the rule; the tests exercise it).

GIVEN
    `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `establishment`                                       IS A STRING
    `assigned there for international tasks`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `activity listed in section 30c(4)`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `overtime hours this month`                            IS A NUMBER
    `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Soldier`
`the soldier who` `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence` `establishment` `assigned there for international tasks` `activity listed in section 30c(4)` `overtime hours this month` `hours blocked by compelling service reasons` MEANS
    `Soldier` WITH
        `serves within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence` IS `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`
        `establishment` IS `establishment`
        `has been transferred or assigned there to perform international or supranational tasks` IS `assigned there for international tasks`
        `is performing an activity listed in section 30c subsection 4` IS `activity listed in section 30c(4)`
        `overtime hours ordered or approved this month` IS `overtime hours this month`
        `hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible` IS `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`
        `has a long-term working-time account` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no question in this layer reads it

§ `Do the working-time rules of the Soldiers Act apply to me?`
@export Do § 30c(1) to (3) of the Soldiers Act, which give time off for overtime, apply to me, reading the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as it is printed? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you serve within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
    `establishment`                                       IS A STRING  @desc The name of the military establishment where you are posted, exactly as the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation prints it, for example Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command; an empty text if you are not posted to one.
    `assigned there for international tasks`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you were transferred or assigned to that establishment to perform international or supranational tasks.
    `activity listed in section 30c(4)`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the work in question is an activity listed in § 30c(4) of the Soldiers Act, such as an operation, disaster relief or a multi-day sea voyage.
    `overtime hours this month`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of officially ordered or approved overtime you worked this month, beyond your regular working time.
    `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`          IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible to give you; 0 if none.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`do the working time rules apply to me under the annex as printed` MEANS
    `section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence` `establishment` `assigned there for international tasks` `activity listed in section 30c(4)` `overtime hours this month` `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`)

@export Do § 30c(1) to (3) of the Soldiers Act, which give time off for overtime, apply to me, if the 2025 listing of my establishment in the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 30c(6) of the Soldiers Act? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you serve within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
    `establishment`                                       IS A STRING  @desc The name of the military establishment where you are posted, exactly as the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation prints it, for example Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command; an empty text if you are not posted to one.
    `assigned there for international tasks`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you were transferred or assigned to that establishment to perform international or supranational tasks.
    `activity listed in section 30c(4)`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the work in question is an activity listed in § 30c(4) of the Soldiers Act, such as an operation, disaster relief or a multi-day sea voyage.
    `overtime hours this month`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of officially ordered or approved overtime you worked this month, beyond your regular working time.
    `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`          IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible to give you; 0 if none.
    `an exception applies`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 listing stands: false assumes none applies and the listing is void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`do the working time rules apply to me if the 2025 listing is void` MEANS
    `section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` (`the reading of the annex to apply` `an exception applies`) (`the soldier who` `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence` `establishment` `assigned there for international tasks` `activity listed in section 30c(4)` `overtime hours this month` `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`)

-- The next group only arises if the soldier is posted to the establishment the article says the 2025 regulation added (Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command).
-- A form can ask "Are you posted to JSEC?" before showing it.
§ `Time off for my overtime`
@export How many hours of time off must I be given for the overtime I worked this month, reading the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as it is printed? Answers a number of hours, from § 30c(2) of the Soldiers Act.
GIVEN
    `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you serve within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
    `establishment`                                       IS A STRING  @desc The name of the military establishment where you are posted, exactly as the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation prints it, for example Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command; an empty text if you are not posted to one.
    `assigned there for international tasks`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you were transferred or assigned to that establishment to perform international or supranational tasks.
    `activity listed in section 30c(4)`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the work in question is an activity listed in § 30c(4) of the Soldiers Act, such as an operation, disaster relief or a multi-day sea voyage.
    `overtime hours this month`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of officially ordered or approved overtime you worked this month, beyond your regular working time.
    `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`          IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible to give you; 0 if none.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many hours of time off must I be given under the annex as printed` MEANS
    `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence` `establishment` `assigned there for international tasks` `activity listed in section 30c(4)` `overtime hours this month` `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`)

@export How many hours of time off must I be given for the overtime I worked this month, if the 2025 listing of my establishment in the annex is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 30c(6) of the Soldiers Act? Answers a number of hours.
GIVEN
    `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you serve within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
    `establishment`                                       IS A STRING  @desc The name of the military establishment where you are posted, exactly as the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation prints it, for example Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command; an empty text if you are not posted to one.
    `assigned there for international tasks`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you were transferred or assigned to that establishment to perform international or supranational tasks.
    `activity listed in section 30c(4)`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the work in question is an activity listed in § 30c(4) of the Soldiers Act, such as an operation, disaster relief or a multi-day sea voyage.
    `overtime hours this month`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of officially ordered or approved overtime you worked this month, beyond your regular working time.
    `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`          IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible to give you; 0 if none.
    `an exception applies`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 listing stands: false assumes none applies and the listing is void.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many hours of time off must I be given if the 2025 listing is void` MEANS
    `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` (`the reading of the annex to apply` `an exception applies`) (`the soldier who` `serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence` `establishment` `assigned there for international tasks` `activity listed in section 30c(4)` `overtime hours this month` `hours blocked by compelling service reasons`)

§ `By when must the time off be given?`
@export Within how many months of the overtime must I be given the time off? Answers 12, or 6 where the shorter period for soldiers in the armed forces has been set (§ 30c(2) sentences 3 and 4 of the Soldiers Act).
GIVEN
    `shorter period set`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the shorter period of six months for soldiers in the armed forces has been set for you; false if not or if you do not know.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`within how many months must the time off be given` MEANS
    `the months within which time off must be given` `shorter period set`

§ `Did the 2025 amending regulation cite the power to exempt my establishment?`
@export Does the preamble of the Regulation of 6 March 2025 that recast the annex to § 1(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation cite § 30c(6) with § 93(2) no. 7 of the Soldiers Act, the power to exempt soldiers at multinational establishments? Answers yes or no, from the gazette text of the preamble.
`does the 2025 preamble cite the power to exempt` MEANS
    `the preamble cites the power`
        `the power needed to exempt a group of soldiers`
        `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`
